{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012wh3mCVBUtYSawCait9Ku5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\tpackage main\n5\t\n6\timport (\n7\t\t\"os/exec\"\n8\t\t\"testing\"\n9\t\n10\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n11\t)\n12\t\n13\tfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n14\t\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n15\t\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gfalse\")\n16\t\tif err != nil {\n17\t\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n18\t\t}\n19\t\tdiscardStdout := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n20\t\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n21\t\t\t{\n22\t\t\t\tName:     \"no-args\",\n23\t\t\t\tExitCode: 1,\n24\t\t\t},\n25\t\t\t{\n26\t\t\t\tName:     \"arbitrary-args\",\n27\t\t\t\tArgs:     []string{\"foo\", \"bar\", \"--baz\"},\n28\t\t\t\tExitCode: 1,\n29\t\t\t},\n30\t\t\t{\n31\t\t\t\tName:      \"help\",\n32\t\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"--help\"},\n33\t\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n34\t\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n35\t\t\t},\n36\t\t\t{\n37\t\t\t\tName:      \"version\",\n38\t\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"--version\"},\n39\t\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n40\t\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n41\t\t\t},\n42\t\t}\n43\t\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n44\t}\n45\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HgCVxzCk5jzb7z27gHYezy","session_id":"511b343f-183f-43d2-9057-b40c12329ec0","uuid":"7005acc9-603b-4780-8ba9-d0d6ce8cd813","timestamp":"2026-05-15T15:20:12.610Z"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a3d1e550674357a6e","tool_use_id":"toolu_01HgCVxzCk5jzb7z27gHYezy","status":"completed","output_file":"","summary":"Find stderr normalizer patterns","usage":{"total_tokens":53477,"tool_uses":32,"duration_ms":90517},"uuid":"7c75b9c7-d446-401f-bb6e-0196e42774aa","session_id":"511b343f-183f-43d2-9057-b40c12329ec0"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HgCVxzCk5jzb7z27gHYezy","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Summary: DiffTest Stderr Normalization Patterns\n\nI've analyzed the repository's differential test framework and found comprehensive patterns for handling stderr normalization when Go implementations differ from GNU reference binaries.\n\n### Core Normalizer Type Definition\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5285/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\n```go\ntype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n```\n\n- Named type alias (R1.4 in spec) for normalization functions\n- Applied in order to both stdout and stderr of both binaries before comparison\n- Part of the `DiffTest` struct as a slice: `Normalize []NormalizeFunc`\n\n### Built-in Normalizer in testutils\n\n**TimestampNormalizer** (for timestamp-producing utilities):\n- Replaces three timestamp patterns: syslog format, ISO format, and time-only\n- Uses regex patterns to normalize to `<TIMESTAMP>` placeholder\n- Used in `cmd/ts` tests\n\n**ComposeNormalizers** utility function:\n- Chains multiple normalizers together in order\n- Useful for combining binary name, case, and quoting normalizers\n\n### Command-Specific Normalizer Patterns\n\n#### 1. Binary Name Normalization (Most Common)\n\n**Pattern:** Across nearly all error-handling test cases\n```go\nbinaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?binaryname`)\nnormalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n    return binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"binaryname\"))\n})\n```\n\n**Why:** Error messages include the binary path (e.g., `/usr/bin/gls` vs `/path/to/ls`). The regex pattern matches both `gls` and plain `ls` with optional path prefix, normalizing to a single canonical name.\n\n**Used in:**\n- `cmd/basename/basename_test.go` - error cases (ExitCode: 1)\n- `cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go` - error cases (ExitCode: 1)  \n- `cmd/hostname/hostname_test.go` - error cases (ExitCode: 1)\n- `cmd/hostid/hostid_test.go` - error cases (ExitCode: 1)\n- `cmd/logname/logname_test.go` - error cases (ExitCode: 1)\n- `cmd/nproc/nproc_test.go` - error cases\n- `cmd/pwd/pwd_test.go` - error cases\n- `cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go` - error cases + multi-operand warning\n- `cmd/realpath/realpath_test.go` - error cases\n- `cmd/seq/seq_test.go` - error cases\n- `cmd/tac/tac_test.go` - error cases\n- `cmd/tty/tty_test.go` - error cases\n- `cmd/uname/uname_test.go` - error cases\n- `cmd/wc/wc_test.go` - error cases\n- `cmd/ls/ls_test.go` - error cases\n\n#### 2. Case Normalization for Error Messages\n\n**Pattern:** When Go and GNU have different capitalization\n```go\nnormalizeErrCase := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n    return bytes.ToLower(b)\n})\n```\n\n**Used in:**\n- `cmd/wc/wc_test.go` - Combined with binary name normalizer for file-not-found errors (ExitCode: 1)\n  ```go\n  Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName, normalizeErrCase}\n  ```\n\n- `cmd/realpath/realpath_test.go` - Lower-cased error messages\n  ```go\n  lowerStderr := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n      return bytes.ToLower(b)\n  })\n  errNorm := []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName, lowerStderr}\n  ```\n\n**Why:** GNU utilities may capitalize differently (\"Error\" vs \"error\", \"No such file\" vs \"no such file\").\n\n#### 3. Quote and Apostrophe Normalization\n\n**Pattern:** When GNU and Go differ in quotation marks\n```go\nnormalizeErrors := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n    s := strings.ToLower(string(b))\n    s = strings.ReplaceAll(s, \"'\", \"\")\n    s = strings.ReplaceAll(s, \"`\", \"\")\n    return []byte(s)\n})\n```\n\n**Used in:**\n- `cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go` - Error normalization removes both single quotes and backticks, plus lowercases\n  ```go\n  errorNorm := []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName, normalizeErrors}\n  ```\n\n**Why:** GNU readlink may quote filenames with backticks or single quotes; Go may use different quoting styles.\n\n#### 4. Output Discarding Normalizers\n\n**Pattern:** When help/version output differs between implementations\n```go\ndiscardStdout := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\ndiscardStderr := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n```\n\n**Used in:**\n- `cmd/basename/basename_test.go` - For `--help` and `--version` flags\n- `cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go` - For `--help` and `--version` flags\n- `cmd/false/false_test.go` - For `--help` (ExitCode: 1) and `--version` (ExitCode: 1)\n- `cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go` - For `--help` and `--version` flags\n- `cmd/realpath/realpath_test.go` - For `--help` and `--version` flags\n- `cmd/tac/tac_test.go` - For discarding stderr when comparing file operations\n\n**Why:** Help and version text is implementation-specific; the exit code is what matters.\n\n### ExitCode: 1 Test Cases with Normalization\n\nThe following commands have test cases with non-zero exit codes that use normalizers:\n\n1. **cmd/false/false_test.go** - All cases (no-args, arbitrary-args, help, version) have `ExitCode: 1`\n   - Uses `discardStdout` normalizer for help/version\n\n2. **cmd/wc/wc_test.go** - File-not-found cases:\n   - `r6_2_nonexistent_file_only` through `r6_2_nonexistent_flag_w`\n   - All use: `[normalizeBinaryName, normalizeErrCase]`\n\n3. **cmd/basename/basename_test.go**:\n   - `error-no-args` (ExitCode: 1) → uses `normalizeBinaryName`\n   - `error-extra-operand` (ExitCode: 1) → uses `normalizeBinaryName`\n\n4. **cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go**:\n   - `no_args_error` (ExitCode: 1) → uses `normalizeBinaryName`\n   - `unknown_option` (ExitCode: 1) → uses `normalizeBinaryName`\n\n5. **cmd/hostname/hostname_test.go**:\n   - `error-extra-operand` (ExitCode: 1) → uses `normalizeBinaryName`\n   - `error-unknown-flag` (ExitCode: 1) → uses `normalizeBinaryName`\n\n6. **cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go**:\n   - Error cases with ExitCode: 1 → uses `[normalizeBinaryName, normalizeErrors]`\n   - `non-symlink`, `directory`, `f-missing-parent`, `e-missing` → `errorNorm`\n\n7. **cmd/logname/logname_test.go**:\n   - `extra_operand` (ExitCode: 1) → uses `normalizeBinaryName`\n   - `unknown_flag` (ExitCode: 1) → uses `normalizeBinaryName`\n\n### Normalization Application Flow\n\nFrom `applyNormalizers()` in difftest.go:\n```go\nfunc applyNormalizers(res binaryResult, fns []NormalizeFunc) binaryResult {\n    for _, fn := range fns {\n        res.stdout = fn(res.stdout)\n        res.stderr = fn(res.stderr)\n    }\n    return res\n}\n```\n\n- Normalizers apply to BOTH stdout AND stderr\n- Applied in sequential order before comparison\n- Each normalizer receives output from previous normalizer\n\n### Key Design Insights\n\n1. **Binary Path Variance**: The `g?binaryname` regex handles both GNU variants (`gls`, `gwc`) and standard names (`ls`, `wc`)\n\n2. **Locale Handling**: Tests consistently set `LC_ALL=C` environment variable to ensure consistent error message formatting across platforms\n\n3. **Stderr Focus**: When Go and GNU produce different stderr messages (case differences, quote styles, path differences), normalizers ensure semantic equivalence is tested rather than exact string matching\n\n4. **Help/Version Strategy**: Rather than normalize help/version output (which is intentionally different), these outputs are discarded entirely, focusing the test on exit code equivalence\n\n5. **Composable Normalizers**: Multiple normalizers can be chained to handle multiple dimensions of variation (binary name + case + quotes)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"511b343f-183f-43d2-9057-b40c12329ec0","uuid":"620117ec-32f2-45cb-b2b3-9cae2610b554","timestamp":"2026-05-15T15:20:32.148Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp4000