n```go\nnormalizeErrors := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n    s := strings.ToLower(string(b))\n    s = strings.ReplaceAll(s, \"'\", \"\")\n    s = strings.ReplaceAll(s, \"`\", \"\")\n    return []byte(s)\n})\n```\n\n**Used in:**\n- `cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go` - Error normalization removes both single quotes and backticks, plus lowercases\n  ```go\n  errorNorm := []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName, normalizeErrors}\n  ```\n\n**Why:** GNU readlink may quote filenames with backticks or single quotes; Go may use different quoting styles.\n\n#### 4. Output Discarding Normalizers\n\n**Pattern:** When help/version output differs between implementations\n```go\ndiscardStdout := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\ndiscardStderr := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n```\n\n**Used in:**\n- `cmd/basename/basename_test.go` - For `--help` and `--version` flags\n- `cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go` - For `--help` and `--version` flags\n- `cmd/false/false_test.go` - For `--help` (ExitCode: 1) and `--version` (ExitCode: 1)\n- `cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go` - For `--help` and `--version` flags\n- `cmd/realpath/realpath_test.go` - For `--help` and `--version` flags\n- `cmd/tac/tac_test.go` - For discarding stderr when comparing file operations\n\n**Why:** Help and version text is implementation-specific; the exit code is what matters.\n\n### ExitCode: 1 Test Cases with Normalization\n\nThe following commands have test cases with non-zero exit codes that use normalizers:\n\n1. **cmd/false/false_test.go** - All cases (no-args, arbitrary-args, help, version) have `ExitCode: 1`\n   - Uses `discardStdout` normalizer for help/version\n\n2. **cmd/wc/wc_test.go** - File-not-found cases:\n   - `r6_2_nonexistent_file_only` through `r6_2_nonexistent_flag_w`\n   - All use: `[normalizeBinaryName, normalizeErrCase]`\n\n3. **cmd/basename/basename_test.go**:\n   - `error-no-args` (ExitCode: 1) → uses `normalizeBinaryName`